  "leakage_audit_md": "# Leakage audit\n\nGenerated by `scripts/leakage_audit.py` on the full cleaned catalogue.\nNormalised mutual information uses `normalized_mutual_info_score` (arithmetic mean).\nCramer's V is computed on the same discrete version of the feature (quantile bins for numerics).\nLogistic accuracy and ROC-AUC are **5-fold out-of-fold** scores of a one-column model.\nThe decision-stump accuracy is in-sample, because a depth-1 tree is the association diagnostic.\nA single feature with ROC-AUC above about 0.97 is treated as a leak.\n\n## Scores\n\n| feature | kind | NMI | Cramer's V | stump accuracy | logistic accuracy | logistic ROC-AUC | note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| duration (raw string) | categorical | 0.2547 | 1.0000 | 0.8834 | 0.9974 | 1.0000 | Perfect separator candidate. |\n| duration_unit | categorical | 1.0000 | 0.9997 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | min versus season. |\n| duration_minutes | numeric | 0.4337 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | Null pattern is the label. |\n| duration_seasons | numeric | 0.8763 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | Null pattern is the label. |\n| duration_minutes_is_null | categorical | 1.0000 | 0.9997 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | Missingness restates the label. |\n| genre_has_banned_tv_token | categorical | 1.0000 | 0.9997 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | 1.0000 | Genre name contains a banned TV-format token. |\n| rating | categorical | 0.0683 | 0.3447 | 0.6969 | 0.7082 | 0.6387 | Partial leak. Quarantined pending this table. |\n| has_director | categorical | 0.6927 | 0.8853 | 0.9520 | 0.9520 | 0.8960 | Films list a director; series often do not. |\n| primary_country | categorical | 0.0603 | 0.4403 | 0.6969 | 0.7561 | 0.6977 | Allowed categorical, audited anyway. |\n| country_is_missing | categorical | 0.0100 | 0.0787 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5105 | Missingness of country. |\n| n_genres | numeric | 0.0068 | 0.0938 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5417 | Count only. Names are banned. |\n| n_countries | numeric | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5105 | Allowed numeric. |\n| release_year | numeric | 0.0216 | 0.2425 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.3522 | Allowed numeric. |\n| year_added | numeric | 0.0019 | 0.0638 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.4911 | Allowed numeric. |\n| month_added | numeric | 0.0035 | 0.0930 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5390 | Allowed numeric. |\n| years_to_platform | numeric | 0.0258 | 0.2401 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.6154 | year_added - release_year. |\n| title_word_count | numeric | 0.0032 | 0.0841 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5261 | Allowed numeric. |\n| description_word_count | numeric | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.4998 | Zero when the source has no synopsis. |\n| n_cast | numeric | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.4998 | Zero when the source has no cast column. |\n| title_has_format_word | categorical | 0.0003 | 0.0141 | 0.6969 | 0.6969 | 0.5007 | Soft cue inside the title. Allowed, ablated in the no-TV-vocabulary track. |\n\n## Crosstabs\n\n### duration_unit\n| value | Movie | TV Show | total |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| min | 6126 | 0 | 6126 |\n| season | 0 | 2664 | 2664 |\n\n### rating\n| value | Movie | TV Show | total |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| TV-MA | 2062 | 1143 | 3205 |\n| TV-14 | 1427 | 730 | 2157 |\n| TV-PG | 540 | 321 | 861 |\n| R | 797 | 2 | 799 |\n| PG-13 | 490 | 0 | 490 |\n| TV-Y7 | 139 | 194 | 333 |\n| TV-Y | 131 | 175 | 306 |\n| PG | 287 | 0 | 287 |\n\n### has_director (1 = a director is listed)\n| value | Movie | TV Show | total |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.0 | 5953 | 249 | 6202 |\n| 0.0 | 173 | 2415 | 2588 |\n\n### genre_has_banned_tv_token\n| value | Movie | TV Show | total |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0.0 | 6126 | 0 | 6126 |\n| 1.0 | 0 | 2664 | 2664 |\n\n### n_genres\n| value | Movie | TV Show | total |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| (0.999, 2.0] | 3717 | 1347 | 5064 |\n| (2.0, 3.0] | 2409 | 1317 | 3726 |\n\n## Verdicts\n\n### Banned\n\n- `duration` raw string, logistic ROC-AUC 1.0000. `90 min` is a movie and `2 Seasons` is a TV show. The string is the label.\n- `duration_unit`, logistic ROC-AUC 1.0000. This is the same fact, parsed. The leaky baseline is the only model allowed to use it, and that model is not served.\n- `duration_minutes` (AUC 1.0000) and `duration_seasons` (AUC 1.0000). Which of the two is non-null is the label. The numeric audit keeps a missingness indicator so imputation cannot hide that.\n- `duration_minutes_is_null`, AUC 1.0000. A missingness flag that restates the unit.\n- Banned TV-format genre tokens, flag AUC 1.0000. Names such as `TV Dramas`, `Docuseries`, and `International TV Shows` are catalogue labels, not content. The honest model receives `n_genres` only.\n\n### Quarantine decisions\n\n- `rating` logistic ROC-AUC is 0.6387: **ALLOWED after quarantine**. `TV-Y`, `TV-Y7`, `TV-Y7-FV`, `TV-G`, `NR`, and `UR` skew toward TV, while `TV-MA` and `TV-14` appear on both classes. The 0.97 single-feature line is the ban threshold.\n- `has_director` logistic ROC-AUC is 0.8960. BANNED. Single-feature accuracy is 0.9520 and Cramer's V is 0.8853. ROC-AUC can sit under the 0.97 perfect-separator line because the feature is binary and the classes are unbalanced, but the decision rule is still a catalogue-missingness detector: series usually have no director credit and films usually do. `features.use_has_director` is false. This extract uses the placeholder `Not Given` for most series and almost no films. Keeping that placeholder as a token would be the second-order leak the spec warns about, so cleaning maps it to missing and the boolean is then judged on its own AUC.\n\n### Allowed, with the ablation\n\n- Title text, including format words. The boolean `title_has_format_word` has AUC 0.5007. The no-TV-vocabulary track strips a fixed 20-word stoplist before TF-IDF so the reader can see how much of the score was the word `series` or `movie`. This extract has no synopsis column, so that ablation runs on the title.\n- `n_genres` AUC 0.5417. The count is kept when it is far from a separator. The names are not used either way.\n- `primary_country` AUC 0.6977, `release_year` AUC 0.3522, `years_to_platform` AUC 0.6154.\n- `description_word_count` AUC 0.4998 and `n_cast` AUC 0.4998. On this extract both columns were absent from the Excel file, so the features are constant and are not passed to the honest model. A file that actually contains them will pick them up.\n\n### What the honest model is allowed to see\n\n`title` (TF-IDF), `primary_country`, `rating`, `release_year`, `year_added`, `month_added`, `years_to_platform`, `n_genres`, `n_countries`, `title_word_count`. Nothing derived from `duration`. No genre name.\n",
